  "content": {
    "en": {
      "overviewMd": "#### A Note from the Founder (Jacksenn)\n\n> \"The very first words you speak in a new language are the most important. They break the ice, they show respect, and they open doors. When I first arrived in Montenegro, I was terrified to speak. But the moment I said 'Dobar dan' to a shopkeeper and she smiled back, I knew I was on the right path. This unit is about giving you those first essential words—the ones that will make you feel human, not helpless. Don't worry about perfection. Just say hello, say thank you, and watch the magic happen.\"\n\n#### Learning Objectives\n\nBy the end of this unit, **we** will be able to:\n\n1. **Greet people** in formal and informal situations using appropriate Serbian phrases.\n2. **Say goodbye** politely.\n3. **Be polite** by using \"thank you,\" \"please,\" and \"excuse me.\"\n4. **Overcome the language barrier** by saying \"I don't speak Serbian\" and \"Do you speak English?\"\n5. **Say yes and no** confidently.\n6. **Introduce ourselves** with our name (very basic).\n\n---",
      "grammarMd": "### A. Verb \"biti\" (to be) - The Essential Forms\n\nWe will learn the **three most important forms** of the verb **\"biti\" (to be)** in this unit. The full conjugation comes in Unit 2.\n\n#### Conjugation Table (Partial)\n\n| Person | Serbian | English |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Ja** | sam | I am |\n| **Ti** | si | You are (informal) |\n| **On/Ona/Ono** | je | He/She/It is |\n\n**Examples:**\n- Ja sam Alex. (I am Alex.)\n- Ja sam turista. (I am a tourist.)\n- Ti si iz Engleske? (Are you from England?)\n- On je konobar. (He is a waiter.)\n- Ona je turistkinja. (She is a tourist.)\n\n**Note:** In casual speech, \"Ja\" and \"Ti\" are often dropped: \"Sam Alex.\" \"Si turista?\" But for beginners, it's safer to include the pronoun.\n\n---\n\n### B. \"Govorim...\" (I speak...) - Overcoming the Language Barrier\n\nWe will learn only the **1st person singular** of the verb **\"govoriti\" (to speak)**.\n\n**Form:** Govorim\n\n**Examples:**\n- Govorim engleski. (I speak English.)\n- Ne govorim srpski. (I don't speak Serbian.)\n\n**Negative Form:** Just add **\"ne\"** before the verb.\n\n---",
      "phrasesMd": "This section combines our new vocabulary into real-world phrases and short dialogues.\n\n### A. Essential Survival Phrases\n\n| Situation | Serbian Phrase | English Translation |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Greeting (informal) | Zdravo! | Hello! |\n| Greeting (formal) | Dobar dan! | Good day! |\n| Greeting (morning) | Dobro jutro! | Good morning! |\n| Greeting (evening) | Dobro veče*! | Good evening! |\n| Saying goodbye | Doviđenja! | Goodbye! |\n| Saying good night | Laku noć! | Good night! |\n| Saying thank you | Hvala! | Thank you! |\n| Saying please | Molim! | Please! |\n| Saying excuse me | Izvinite! | Excuse me! |\n| Saying yes | Da! | Yes! |\n| Saying no | Ne! | No! |\n| I don't speak Serbian | Ne govorim srpski. | I don't speak Serbian. |\n| I speak English | Govorim engleski. | I speak English. |\n| Do you speak English? | Govorite li engleski? | Do you speak English? |\n| I understand | Razumem*. | I understand. |\n| I don't understand | Ne razumem*. | I don't understand. |\n| I am... (name) | Ja sam... | I am... |\n\n*Montenegro: Dobro veče (same), Razumijem, Ne razumijem\n\n---",
      "dialoguesMd": "",
      "testIntroductionMd": "**We** will use these exercises to solidify our understanding of the absolute basics."
    }
  },
